// the class-member lookup, which is the one place that knows both the receiver
// and its class. A staticmethod yields the plain function; a classmethod yields
// it bound to a class - and to the class of the RECEIVER, so a subclass instance
// passes the subclass as cls, which is what makes alternative constructors work.
